Rules:
  [N1] Use ASP.NET Core for web APIs.
  [N2] Use Entity Framework Core for data.
  [N3] Use dependency injection.
  [N4] Use minimal APIs for simple endpoints.
  [N5] Use controllers for complex APIs.
  [N6] Use middleware for cross-cutting.
  [N7] Use ILogger for logging.
  [N8] Use appsettings.json for config.

Pros:
  - Excellent performance
  - Strong typing
  - Cross-platform

Cons:
  - Memory usage
  - Ecosystem fragmentation
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Go (simpler)
  - Java (similar)
  - Node.js (lighter)

